# Codebase style

**Mandatory** when editing application code (`rules.follow_existing_codebase_style`).

1. Read `docs/conventions/code-style.md` and `.project/conventions.yaml` (naming: camelCase variables/functions, PascalCase classes, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE constants, kebab-case files — or match this repo if different).
2. Read `docs/conventions/structure.md` for folder layout.
3. Read adjacent files first; match their patterns.
4. Do not introduce new frameworks, naming styles, or folder layouts unless asked or an ADR requires it.

Preflight prints active naming rules — run `node scripts/ledger.mjs preflight` before coding.
